      children: "Multi-stage generation achieves the highest schema adherence rates of the three patterns-often exceeding 99.5%-because it never requires the model to satisfy all constraints simultaneously. The decomposition strategy reduces cognitive load on the model in the same way that breaking complex functions into smaller functions reduces cognitive load for developers. Each stage operates in a constrained context where success criteria are clear and limited. This clarity translates directly to higher success rates."
